& [Purpose]
  + add one official-rmcp read-only semantic inspection tool for an ephemeral bounded caller-owned SDK session while leaving existing wire stdio consumer and semantics code unchanged
  + expose exact original wire response JSON as a string in structuredContent rather than parse and reserialize its semantic bytes or mislabel MCP as the EOF host contract

& [SelectedBoundary]
  + new safe-Rust cantor_sop_inspect_mcp crate and zero-argument cantor-sop-inspect-mcp native executable
  + one inspect_sop_semantics tool receives exactly one wire_request_json string argument after SDK normalization and delegates to unchanged strict wire parsing/responding
  + three typed reply outcomes inspection_succeeded semantic_refused adapter_refused retain raw request/result byte counts SHA256 exact response JSON optional fixed fault code and non-authority
  + semantic and adapter refusal use MCP is_error true while valid semantic result uses false; unknown tool uses official method-not-found
  + tools-only server metadata declares readonly non-destructive idempotent closed-world operation; no resources roots sampling providers models or arbitrary command tools
  + duplicate-key behavior of the MCP envelope remains official SDK behavior; only the retained nested wire bytes are strictly duplicate-rejecting
  + no new ConsumerReceipt is issued for MCP because its session framing differs from the zero-argument EOF transcript contract

& [FixedP0SafetyCeilings]
  + decoded wire request262144 bytes wire response1048576 bytes
  + input MCP frame2097152 bytes output MCP frame4194304 bytes
  + aggregate input8388608 bytes plus one overflow witness aggregate reserved output8388608 bytes
  + at most32 decoded messages including initialization and notifications and at most one active semantic call with fail-closed busy refusal rather than a product queue
  + whole native session60 seconds runtime shutdown wait250 milliseconds two async workers and at most two blocking stdio workers
  + this is an ephemeral P0 SDK session not an indefinitely registered/resident agent service; independent application owns trusted launch restart longer-lived integration and acceptance

& [TransportAndNativeMechanism]
  + use installed official SDK JsonRpcMessageCodec with explicit decoder bound and FramedRead/FramedWrite through the SDK Transport trait; do not fork MCP parser dispatch or protocol models
  + enforce actual aggregate raw input count decoded-message ceiling encoded output frame ceiling and checked aggregate output reservation; flag and cancel on every budget codec or output fault
  + inherited MCP codec behavior includes compatibility notifications BOM and complete-value EOF; do not invent stricter external framing claims or assume closing stdin guarantees completion of asynchronous requests
  + native main rejects extra arguments with fixed non-echoing public fault and exit2; initialized normal client disconnect exits0; protocol/handshake/budget/output/deadline failure exits2 with fixed cantor_semantic_inspection_mcp_refused newline
  + standalone runtime enforces session deadline and explicit shutdown_timeout before process exit; no default runtime drop that can wait indefinitely for stdio workers
  + prefer safe duplication of already-inherited stdin/stdout handles or descriptors into File wrappers without any pathname open create metadata directory or arbitrary-handle API; this avoids global Stdout LineWriter buffering in the SDK data path
  + stdin/stdout handle duplication stdio reads/writes transport bookkeeping and deadline clock are newly delineated adapter effects; they are not silently imported from the pure consumer signature
  + runtime shutdown can leave blocking stdio work until process termination; library generic I/O helpers do not claim to kill a caller's runtime or external process

